// kyoten::input — devices into a game's actions (the first slice's step 8, KYR-54; design/input.md § Decided). The
// binder reads the bindings records and the samples a platform hands in, and makes each owed step's hand-off: every
// player's action values, split by each sample's time.
//
// - **Bindings are content,** keyed by action, then device (question 2): a control's name, a list of them, or an object
//   of an action kind's parts, by `@kama/window`'s names (`"ArrowUp"`, `"RightShoulder"`, `"LeftX"`), each read by the
//   package's own reader, so a misspelling is refused at load with every name listed. The mouse's motion is kyoten's
//   own: `"Motion"` for a `Vector2`, `"MotionX"` and `"MotionY"` for one axis. An object's gestures are refused by name
//   until KYR-54's later part reads them.
// - **An entry's filters** (the third part, design/input.md § Decided, 2026-11-23) reshape the value its parts make, in
//   the order written, before a delta's seconds, on a step's hand-off and on Output's newest alike: `deadZone`, `scale`,
//   `invert`, `curve`, `clamp`, `remap`, `normalize`, `digital` and `smooth`, whose state each path keeps apart. On the
//   mouse's motion, a distance moved, only `scale`, `invert` and `smooth`, since the rest would change with the step's
//   length; `smooth` smooths its speed. A value out of its filter's range is refused at load, naming the action.
// - **Split by time** (question 1): a step takes the samples that arrived by its end and were not handed off yet, so a
//   frame that owes no step keeps its input for the next.
// - **Player 1** has the keyboard and the mouse throughout, and **the first pad pressed**, locked until it disconnects
//   (question 4): while one is locked another pad does nothing. A pad takes the lock with a button pressed, never a
//   stick or a trigger's travel alone, so a drifting or knocked stick cannot take player 1.
// - **One action on several controls** (`["ArrowUp", "KeyW"]`) is held while any of them is, and its edges are those
//   of that combined state.
// - **Edges, per step** (kyoten::frame::Digital): a press and its release inside one step show the press, held, on that
//   step and the release on the next; a release and a press inside one step show both, held.
// - **A control is on at `Gamepad::PressedAt` of its travel or more,** `@kama/window`'s own threshold, for every device.
// - **The default dead zones** (the third part's question 1): the `input` record's, every layer's laid over, given to
//   every stick an entry reads and every trigger's travel unless the entry's own filters name a `deadZone`: radial,
//   before its own filters, where the entry reads both axes of one stick as its x and y, and on each axis or trigger
//   alone otherwise. A record naming none reads raw.
// - **Player 1's active scheme** (the second part's question 1) is the kind of device that last drove them: a key or a
//   mouse button pressed or the mouse moved is `KeyboardMouse`; the locked pad's button pressed, a trigger past
//   `PressedAt` or a stick past half its travel is `Gamepad`, so drift cannot switch it; the locked pad gone, back to
//   `KeyboardMouse`. Each step's hand-off carries it as of the step's end.
// - **A value action** (`Analog`, `Vector2`, `Vector3`; the second part's questions 1 and 2):
//   - an entry's parts make its value: an `Analog`'s `positive` less its `negative`; a `Vector2`'s `right` less `left`
//     and `up` less `down`, or its `x` and `y`; a `Vector3`'s with `backward` less `forward` (forward is -Z) or `z`.
//     Up is positive on every device: a stick's Y and the mouse's motion down the window are turned over. Keys make a
//     direction no longer than 1, so a diagonal is not faster (Unity's DigitalNormalized, Godot's `get_vector`);
//   - a part on several controls reads the most actuated, and **a state** (any value whose record says no `delta`) the
//     most actuated of its devices' entries, as of the step's end (Unity's default, Godot's strongest);
//   - **a delta** sums them: the mouse's motion that landed in the step, and each control held times the step's
//     seconds, so a stick turns as far each second whatever the rate. The mouse's motion bound to a state is refused.
// - **Output's newest** (`newest`, frame-phases § Decided: "presentation reads, such as camera look, take the newest
//   sample each frame"): every sample taken so far applied, each state as of the newest, each delta since Output's last
//   frame at the frame's seconds, whether or not a step took them. In a frame that owes no step the samples are applied
//   early, which loses nothing: each still lands in the next step's hand-off, since a step's edges and motion are cleared
//   after it is handed off, and every sample taken arrived before the next step's end.
//
// It is tier `Module`, outside the simulation's fence, as the module that reads devices must be, and names
// `kyoten::frame` and `kyoten::records` alone of the engine; the generated `run` builds it and hands it to the loop.

import { std::collections::DynamicArray, std::collections::SortedMap, std::memory::Owned, std::math::Vec2,
         std::math::Vec3, std::math::sqrt, std::serialization::text::json::deserializeJsonBuffer,
         kyoten::frame::Digital, kyoten::frame::Handoff, kyoten::frame::Sample, kyoten::frame::SampleKind,
         kyoten::frame::Device, kyoten::frame::InputSource, kyoten::frame::ActionList, kyoten::frame::Time,
         kyoten::frame::Scheme,
         kyoten::records::BindingRecord, kyoten::records::ControlEntry, kyoten::records::ActionKind,
         kyoten::records::FilterRecord, kyoten::records::FilterKind, kyoten::records::InputRecord, std::math::exp,
         std::math::pow,
         window::Key, window::PadButton, window::PadAxis, window::PointerButton, window::Gamepad };

export { Binder, BindingError };

comptime int32 NO_PAD = -1;
// How far a stick goes before it says the pad is in use: half its travel, so a drifting or knocked stick does not.
comptime float32 STICK_IN_USE = 0.5;

// Why bindings were refused at load: one line each, every refusal at once.
type resource BindingError implements Error {
    DynamicArray<string> linesField = DynamicArray.empty();

    public ctor make() { }

    public fn void add(string line) { this.linesField.add(item: give line); }
    public const fn bool any() { return this.linesField.length() > 0; }
    public const fn const ref DynamicArray<string> lines() { return this.linesField; }
    public const fn string message() {
        string all = "";
        foreach (const ref string l in this.linesField.iterConst()) { all = all.isEmpty() ? copy l : all + "; " + l; }
        return all;
    }
}

// One control a digital action is bound to, and whether it is on.
type value Bound {
    public Device device;
    public int32 control;
    public bool on = false;

    public ctor make(Device device, int32 control) {
        this.device = device;
        this.control = control;
    }
}

// How a value entry's parts make its value.
type enum Shape { One, Pair, Keys2, Axes2, Keys3, Axes3 }

// Which default dead zone a source reads through on its own.
type enum Zone { None, Stick, Trigger }

// One control a value is read from: a key's or a button's edge (1 or 0), a pad button's travel, a stick's axis, or the
// mouse's motion; and what it reads now.
type value Source {
    public Device device;
    public SampleKind kind;
    public int32 control;
    // A Y read up positive: a stick's LeftY or RightY, the mouse's motion down the window.
    public bool flip;
    // As of the last sample taken: a state.
    public float32 value = 0.0;
    // The default dead zone it reads through, per axis: none, a stick's or a trigger's.
    public Zone zone = Zone::None;
    // The mouse's motion since the last hand-off, and since Output's last frame.
    public float32 moved = 0.0;
    public float32 shown = 0.0;

    public ctor make(Device device, SampleKind kind, int32 control, bool flip) {
        this.device = device;
        this.kind = kind;
        this.control = control;
        this.flip = flip;
    }
}

// One device's entry of a value action: its kind and its index there, its shape, whether it is the mouse's motion, its
// parts' sources, part k's from `firsts[k]` up to `firsts[k + 1]` in the binder's sources, and its filters, from
// `filterFrom` up to `filterTo` in the binder's.
type value Entry {
    public ActionKind kind;
    public int32 action;
    public Shape shape;
    public bool motion = false;
    public InlineArray<isize>#(7) firsts;
    public isize filterFrom = 0;
    public isize filterTo = 0;

    public ctor make(ActionKind kind, int32 action, Shape shape) {
        this.kind = kind;
        this.action = action;
        this.shape = shape;
        this.firsts = [0; 7];
    }
}

type resource Binder implements InputSource {
    int32 playerCount;
    int32 digitalCount;
    float32 stepSeconds;
    // Every digital action's controls, action by action: action a's are `controls[firsts[a]]` up to `controls[firsts[a + 1]]`.
    DynamicArray<Bound> controls = DynamicArray.empty();
    DynamicArray<isize> firsts = DynamicArray.empty();
    // Each digital action's combined state as of the last sample handed off, and a tap's release owed to the next step.
    DynamicArray<bool> combined = DynamicArray.empty();
    DynamicArray<bool> owedRelease = DynamicArray.empty();
    // Every value action's entries, and the controls they read.
    DynamicArray<Entry> entries = DynamicArray.empty();
    DynamicArray<Source> sources = DynamicArray.empty();
    // Every value entry's filters, every curve's points in pairs (in, out), and each `smooth`'s value so far on the
    // steps' path and on Output's, by filter.
    DynamicArray<FilterRecord> filters = DynamicArray.empty();
    DynamicArray<float32> points = DynamicArray.empty();
    DynamicArray<Vec3> smoothSteps = DynamicArray.empty();
    DynamicArray<Vec3> smoothShown = DynamicArray.empty();
    // The `input` record's dead zones, where it names them.
    Optional<FilterRecord> stickZone = Optional::None;
    Optional<FilterRecord> triggerZone = Optional::None;
    // Which value actions are deltas, by kind, as the game's `ActionList` says.
    DynamicArray<bool> analogDeltas = DynamicArray.empty();
    DynamicArray<bool> vector2Deltas = DynamicArray.empty();
    DynamicArray<bool> vector3Deltas = DynamicArray.empty();
    // The pad player 1 has locked in, NO_PAD while none, and player 1's active scheme.
    int32 lockSlot = NO_PAD;
    Scheme schemeNow = Scheme::KeyboardMouse;
    // The samples handed in, oldest first, those before `head` handed off; cleared once all are.
    DynamicArray<Sample> waiting = DynamicArray.empty();
    isize head = 0;
    // Each digital action's edges inside the step being handed off.
    DynamicArray<bool> onEdge = DynamicArray.empty();
    DynamicArray<bool> offEdge = DynamicArray.empty();
    Handoff out;
    // What Output reads, and the seconds a held control counts for in a delta: the step's, or Output's frame's.
    Handoff view;
    float32 seconds = 0.0;

    // A binder for `players` players and the game's actions, each kind's named in the generated order, bound by
    // `bindings`, every content layer's merged, with `input`'s defaults; `hz` the base rate, whose step's seconds a
    // control held counts for in a delta. A binding naming no action, a control that names none of its device's, an
    // entry its action's kind cannot read, a filter or a default out of its range, or what KYR-54 does not read yet is
    // refused, every one at once.
    public ctor Result<Binder, BindingError> make(int32 players, const ref ActionList actions,
                                                  const ref SortedMap<string, BindingRecord> bindings,
                                                  const ref InputRecord input, int32 hz) {
        this.playerCount = players;
        this.digitalCount = actions.digitalCount();
        this.stepSeconds = Time::dtAt(hz: hz);
        this.out = Handoff.make(players: players, actions: actions);
        this.view = Handoff.make(players: players, actions: actions);
        BindingError no = BindingError.make();
        DynamicArray<float32> noPoints = DynamicArray.empty();
        match (input.stickDeadZone()) {
            case Some(value: f): {
                string why = filterRefusal(f: f, points: noPoints, motion: false);
                if (why.isEmpty()) { this.stickZone = Optional::Some(value: f); }
                else { no.add(line: "the `input` record's `stickDeadZone` " + why); }
            }
            case None: { }
        };
        match (input.triggerDeadZone()) {
            case Some(value: f): {
                string why = filterRefusal(f: f, points: noPoints, motion: false);
                if (why.isEmpty()) { this.triggerZone = Optional::Some(value: f); }
                else { no.add(line: "the `input` record's `triggerDeadZone` " + why); }
            }
            case None: { }
        };
        foreach (string action in bindings) {
            string kind = kindOf(actions: actions, name: action);
            if (kind.isEmpty()) {
                no.add(line: "the bindings of `" + action + "` name no action: an action is declared in a module's records file");
            } else if (kind == "Pose") {
                no.add(line: "the bindings of `" + action + "` bind a `Pose` action, which no device binds until XR brings one (KYR-34)");
            }
        }
        foreach (const ref string action in actions.digitalNames().iterConst()) {
            this.firsts.add(item: this.controls.length());
            this.combined.add(item: false);
            this.owedRelease.add(item: false);
            this.onEdge.add(item: false);
            this.offEdge.add(item: false);
            if (!bindings.contains(key: action)) { continue; }
            borrow bindings.getRef(key: action) as b {
                this.bindEntry(action: action, device: Device::Keyboard, entry: b.keyboard(), no: no);
                this.bindEntry(action: action, device: Device::Mouse, entry: b.mouse(), no: no);
                this.bindEntry(action: action, device: Device::Gamepad, entry: b.gamepad(), no: no);
            }
        }
        this.firsts.add(item: this.controls.length());
        int32 a = 0;
        while (a < actions.analogCount()) {
            bool delta = actions.analogDelta(action: a);
            this.analogDeltas.add(item: delta);
            this.bindValue(kind: ActionKind::Analog, index: a, name: actions.analogNames()[cast<isize>(a)], delta: delta,
                           bindings: bindings, no: no);
            a = a + 1;
        }
        a = 0;
        while (a < actions.vector2Count()) {
            bool delta = actions.vector2Delta(action: a);
            this.vector2Deltas.add(item: delta);
            this.bindValue(kind: ActionKind::Vector2, index: a, name: actions.vector2Names()[cast<isize>(a)], delta: delta,
                           bindings: bindings, no: no);
            a = a + 1;
        }
        a = 0;
        while (a < actions.vector3Count()) {
            bool delta = actions.vector3Delta(action: a);
            this.vector3Deltas.add(item: delta);
            this.bindValue(kind: ActionKind::Vector3, index: a, name: actions.vector3Names()[cast<isize>(a)], delta: delta,
                           bindings: bindings, no: no);
            a = a + 1;
        }
        if (no.any()) { return Result::Err(error: give no); }
        return Result::Ok(value: give this);
    }

    public const fn int32 players() { return this.playerCount; }
    public const fn int32 digitalActions() { return this.digitalCount; }
    // Player 1's active scheme as of the samples handed off.
    public const fn Scheme scheme() { return this.schemeNow; }
    // The pad slot player 1 has locked in, None while none is.
    public const fn Optional<int32> lockedPad() {
        if (this.lockSlot == NO_PAD) { return Optional::None; }
        return Optional::Some(value: this.lockSlot);
    }
    // How many controls digital action `action` is bound to, for a test to read what was bound.
    public const fn isize boundCount(int32 action) {
        if (action < 0 || action >= this.digitalCount) { return 0; }
        isize a = cast<isize>(action);
        return this.firsts[a + 1] - this.firsts[a];
    }
    // How many entries the value actions have, and how many controls they read, for a test to read what was bound.
    public const fn isize valueEntries() { return this.entries.length(); }
    public const fn isize valueSources() { return this.sources.length(); }

    // The samples a platform handed in since the last call, which arrived in the order of their times.
    public fn void take(const ref DynamicArray<Sample> samples) {
        foreach (Sample s in samples) { this.waiting.add(item: s); }
    }

    // The hand-off of a step, from the samples that arrived by `until` (inclusive, on the frame timestamp's base) and
    // were not handed off yet; the driver hands the frame's last owed step everything that arrived.
    public fn const ref Handoff handoff(int64 index, int64 until) {
        this.out.clear();
        int32 a = 0;
        while (this.head < this.waiting.length() && this.waiting[this.head].at <= until) {
            Sample s = this.waiting[this.head];
            this.apply(s: s);
            this.head = this.head + 1;
        }
        if (this.head == this.waiting.length()) {
            this.waiting.clear();
            this.head = 0;
        }
        a = 0;
        while (a < this.digitalCount) {
            isize i = cast<isize>(a);
            bool now = this.combined[i];
            Digital d = Digital.off();
            if (this.owedRelease[i]) {
                d.released = true;
                this.owedRelease[i] = false;
            }
            if (this.onEdge[i]) {
                d.pressed = true;
                d.held = true;
                if (!now) { this.owedRelease[i] = true; }
                if (this.offEdge[i] && now) { d.released = true; }
            } else if (this.offEdge[i]) {
                d.released = true;
            } else {
                d.held = now;
            }
            if (this.playerCount >= 1) { this.out.setDigital(player: 1, action: a, value: d); }
            a = a + 1;
        }
        if (this.playerCount >= 1) {
            this.seconds = this.stepSeconds;
            this.handValues(forOutput: false);
            this.out.setScheme(player: 1, value: this.schemeNow);
        }
        a = 0;
        while (a < this.digitalCount) {
            this.onEdge[cast<isize>(a)] = false;
            this.offEdge[cast<isize>(a)] = false;
            a = a + 1;
        }
        isize k = 0;
        while (k < this.sources.length()) {
            this.sources[k].moved = 0.0;
            k = k + 1;
        }
        return this.out;
    }

    // What Output reads this frame: every sample taken so far applied, each state as of the newest, each delta since
    // the last call at `seconds`, the frame's, every digital off; the samples' edges and motion kept for the next step.
    public fn const ref Handoff newest(float32 seconds) {
        this.view.clear();
        while (this.head < this.waiting.length()) {
            Sample s = this.waiting[this.head];
            this.apply(s: s);
            this.head = this.head + 1;
        }
        this.waiting.clear();
        this.head = 0;
        if (this.playerCount >= 1) {
            this.seconds = seconds;
            this.handValues(forOutput: true);
            this.view.setScheme(player: 1, value: this.schemeNow);
        }
        isize k = 0;
        while (k < this.sources.length()) {
            this.sources[k].shown = 0.0;
            k = k + 1;
        }
        return this.view;
    }

    // Each value action's value into player 1's hand-off, a step's or Output's: a state's most actuated entry, a
    // delta's sum, a control held counting for `this.seconds`.
    fn void handValues(bool forOutput) {
        isize e = 0;
        while (e < this.entries.length()) {
            Entry entry = this.entries[e];
            Vec3 parts = this.entryValue(e: entry, forOutput: forOutput);
            Vec3 v = this.filtered(e: entry, value: parts, forOutput: forOutput);
            bool delta = this.isDelta(kind: entry.kind, action: entry.action);
            if (delta && !entry.motion) {
                v = Vec3.of(x: v.x * this.seconds, y: v.y * this.seconds, z: v.z * this.seconds);
            }
            match (entry.kind) {
                case Analog: {
                    float32 had = forOutput ? this.view.analog(player: 1, action: entry.action) : this.out.analog(player: 1, action: entry.action);
                    float32 now = delta ? had + v.x : (absOf(x: v.x) > absOf(x: had) ? v.x : had);
                    if (forOutput) { this.view.setAnalog(player: 1, action: entry.action, value: now); }
                    else { this.out.setAnalog(player: 1, action: entry.action, value: now); }
                }
                case Vector2: {
                    Vec2 had = forOutput ? this.view.vector2(player: 1, action: entry.action) : this.out.vector2(player: 1, action: entry.action);
                    Vec2 mine = Vec2.of(x: v.x, y: v.y);
                    Vec2 now = delta ? had + mine : (v.x * v.x + v.y * v.y > had.x * had.x + had.y * had.y ? mine : had);
                    if (forOutput) { this.view.setVector2(player: 1, action: entry.action, value: now); }
                    else { this.out.setVector2(player: 1, action: entry.action, value: now); }
                }
                case Vector3: {
                    Vec3 had = forOutput ? this.view.vector3(player: 1, action: entry.action) : this.out.vector3(player: 1, action: entry.action);
                    Vec3 now = delta ? had + v : (lengthSquared(v: v) > lengthSquared(v: had) ? v : had);
                    if (forOutput) { this.view.setVector3(player: 1, action: entry.action, value: now); }
                    else { this.out.setVector3(player: 1, action: entry.action, value: now); }
                }
                case _: { }
            };
            e = e + 1;
        }
    }

    // An entry's value through its filters, in the order written, each on the axes its kind reads (an `Analog` 1, a
    // `Vector2` 2, a `Vector3` 3), the others held at 0.
    fn Vec3 filtered(Entry e, Vec3 value, bool forOutput) {
        int32 dims = match (e.kind) { case Analog: 1; case Vector2: 2; case _: 3; };
        Vec3 v = value;
        isize i = e.filterFrom;
        while (i < e.filterTo) {
            FilterRecord f = this.filters[i];
            match (f.kind) {
                case DeadZone: { v = deadZoned(v: v, f: f); }
                case Scale: { v = Vec3.of(x: v.x * f.a, y: v.y * f.b, z: v.z * f.c); }
                case Invert: { v = Vec3.of(x: invertedBy(x: v.x, by: f.a), y: invertedBy(x: v.y, by: f.b), z: invertedBy(x: v.z, by: f.c)); }
                case Curve: {
                    if (f.points) {
                        v = Vec3.of(x: this.throughPoints(x: v.x, f: f), y: this.throughPoints(x: v.y, f: f),
                                    z: this.throughPoints(x: v.z, f: f));
                    } else {
                        v = Vec3.of(x: powered(x: v.x, e: f.a), y: powered(x: v.y, e: f.b), z: powered(x: v.z, e: f.c));
                    }
                }
                case Clamp: { v = clampedBy(v: v, f: f); }
                case Remap: { v = Vec3.of(x: remapped(x: v.x, f: f), y: remapped(x: v.y, f: f), z: remapped(x: v.z, f: f)); }
                case Normalize: { if (f.on) { v = unit(v: v); } }
                case Digital: { if (f.on) { v = Vec3.of(x: signOf(x: v.x), y: signOf(x: v.y), z: signOf(x: v.z)); } }
                case Smooth: { v = this.smoothed(i: i, v: v, f: f, motion: e.motion, forOutput: forOutput); }
                case Threshold: { }
            };
            v = masked(v: v, dims: dims);
            i = i + 1;
        }
        return v;
    }

    // A curve through `f`'s points on `x`'s size, linear between them and level past the ends, its sign kept.
    const fn float32 throughPoints(float32 x, FilterRecord f) {
        float32 a = absOf(x: x);
        isize first = f.pointsFrom;
        isize last = f.pointsTo - 2;
        float32 got = this.points[first + 1];
        if (a >= this.points[last]) {
            got = this.points[last + 1];
        } else if (a > this.points[first]) {
            isize k = first;
            while (k < last) {
                float32 x0 = this.points[k];
                float32 x1 = this.points[k + 2];
                if (a <= x1) {
                    float32 y0 = this.points[k + 1];
                    float32 y1 = this.points[k + 3];
                    got = y0 + (a - x0) / (x1 - x0) * (y1 - y0);
                    k = last;
                } else {
                    k = k + 2;
                }
            }
        }
        return x < 0.0 ? 0.0 - got : (x > 0.0 ? got : 0.0);
    }

    // `v` smoothed by `f`'s time: moved toward its value by the share of it `this.seconds` makes, from the path's last
    // value; the mouse's motion as a speed, so how far it moves is kept whatever the step.
    fn Vec3 smoothed(isize i, Vec3 v, FilterRecord f, bool motion, bool forOutput) {
        float32 dt = this.seconds;
        Vec3 had = forOutput ? this.smoothShown[i] : this.smoothSteps[i];
        if (dt <= 0.0) { return motion ? v : had; }
        float32 share = 1.0 - exp(x: 0.0 - dt / f.a);
        Vec3 target = motion ? Vec3.of(x: v.x / dt, y: v.y / dt, z: v.z / dt) : v;
        Vec3 now = Vec3.of(x: had.x + (target.x - had.x) * share, y: had.y + (target.y - had.y) * share,
                           z: had.z + (target.z - had.z) * share);
        if (forOutput) { this.smoothShown[i] = now; } else { this.smoothSteps[i] = now; }
        return motion ? Vec3.of(x: now.x * dt, y: now.y * dt, z: now.z * dt) : now;
    }

    const fn bool isDelta(ActionKind kind, int32 action) {
        isize a = cast<isize>(action);
        return match (kind) {
            case Analog: this.analogDeltas[a];
            case Vector2: this.vector2Deltas[a];
            case Vector3: this.vector3Deltas[a];
            case _: false;
        };
    }

    // An entry's value from its parts, as a three-component value (an `Analog` its x, a `Vector2` its x and y); the
    // mouse's motion since the last step, or since Output's last frame.
    const fn Vec3 entryValue(Entry e, bool forOutput) {
        float32 p0 = this.partValue(e: e, part: 0, forOutput: forOutput);
        float32 p1 = this.partValue(e: e, part: 1, forOutput: forOutput);
        float32 p2 = this.partValue(e: e, part: 2, forOutput: forOutput);
        float32 p3 = this.partValue(e: e, part: 3, forOutput: forOutput);
        float32 p4 = this.partValue(e: e, part: 4, forOutput: forOutput);
        float32 p5 = this.partValue(e: e, part: 5, forOutput: forOutput);
        return match (e.shape) {
            case One: Vec3.of(x: p0, y: 0.0, z: 0.0);
            case Pair: Vec3.of(x: p0 - p1, y: 0.0, z: 0.0);
            case Keys2: clamped(v: Vec3.of(x: p3 - p2, y: p0 - p1, z: 0.0));
            case Axes2: Vec3.of(x: p0, y: p1, z: 0.0);
            case Keys3: clamped(v: Vec3.of(x: p3 - p2, y: p0 - p1, z: p5 - p4));
            case Axes3: Vec3.of(x: p0, y: p1, z: p2);
        };
    }

    // A part's value: the mouse's motion summed, or the most actuated of its controls.
    const fn float32 partValue(Entry e, int32 part, bool forOutput) {
        isize from = e.firsts[cast<isize>(part)];
        isize to = e.firsts[cast<isize>(part) + 1];
        float32 best = 0.0;
        isize i = from;
        while (i < to) {
            Source s = this.sources[i];
            if (s.kind == SampleKind::Motion) { best = best + (forOutput ? s.shown : s.moved); }
            else {
                float32 v = this.zonedSource(s: s);
                if (absOf(x: v) > absOf(x: best)) { best = v; }
            }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        return best;
    }

    // A source's value through its default dead zone, on its own axis.
    const fn float32 zonedSource(Source s) {
        Optional<FilterRecord> zone = match (s.zone) {
            case None: Optional::None;
            case Stick: this.stickZone;
            case Trigger: this.triggerZone;
        };
        return match (zone) {
            case Some(value: f): signOf(x: s.value) * zoned(size: absOf(x: s.value), f: f);
            case None: s.value;
        };
    }

    // One sample: a pad's lock, then each control it moves, then each digital action whose combined state it changes.
    fn void apply(Sample s) {
        match (s.kind) {
            case Connected: { return; }
            case Disconnected: {
                if (s.slot == this.lockSlot) {
                    this.lockSlot = NO_PAD;
                    this.release(device: Device::Gamepad);
                    this.schemeNow = Scheme::KeyboardMouse;
                }
                return;
            }
            case Control: { }
            case Travel: {
                if (s.slot != this.lockSlot) { return; }
                if (s.value >= Gamepad::PressedAt) { this.schemeNow = Scheme::Gamepad; }
                this.setValues(s: s);
                return;
            }
            case Axis: {
                if (s.slot != this.lockSlot) { return; }
                if (absOf(x: s.value) >= STICK_IN_USE) { this.schemeNow = Scheme::Gamepad; }
                this.setValues(s: s);
                return;
            }
            case Motion: {
                this.schemeNow = Scheme::KeyboardMouse;
                this.setValues(s: s);
                return;
            }
        };
        bool on = s.value >= Gamepad::PressedAt;
        if (s.device == Device::Gamepad) {
            if (this.lockSlot == NO_PAD && on) { this.lockSlot = s.slot; }
            if (s.slot != this.lockSlot) { return; }
            if (on) { this.schemeNow = Scheme::Gamepad; }
        } else if (on) {
            this.schemeNow = Scheme::KeyboardMouse;
        }
        isize i = 0;
        while (i < this.controls.length()) {
            if (this.controls[i].device == s.device && this.controls[i].control == s.control) { this.controls[i].on = on; }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        this.setValues(s: s);
        this.settle();
    }

    // Each value source the sample moves: an edge's 1 or 0, a travel or an axis as it reads (a Y turned over), or the
    // mouse's motion added to what it moved this step.
    fn void setValues(Sample s) {
        isize i = 0;
        while (i < this.sources.length()) {
            Source src = this.sources[i];
            if (src.device == s.device && src.kind == s.kind && src.control == s.control) {
                float32 v = s.value;
                if (s.kind == SampleKind::Control) { v = s.value >= Gamepad::PressedAt ? 1.0 : 0.0; }
                if (src.flip) { v = -v; }
                if (s.kind == SampleKind::Motion) {
                    this.sources[i].moved = src.moved + v;
                    this.sources[i].shown = src.shown + v;
                }
                else { this.sources[i].value = v; }
            }
            i = i + 1;
        }
    }

    // Every control of `device` off and at rest: a pad gone with its lock.
    fn void release(Device device) {
        isize i = 0;
        while (i < this.controls.length()) {
            if (this.controls[i].device == device) { this.controls[i].on = false; }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        i = 0;
        while (i < this.sources.length()) {
            if (this.sources[i].device == device) { this.sources[i].value = 0.0; }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        this.settle();
    }

    // Each digital action's combined state from its controls, an edge noted where it changed.
    fn void settle() {
        int32 a = 0;
        while (a < this.digitalCount) {
            isize ai = cast<isize>(a);
            bool any = false;
            isize c = this.firsts[ai];
            while (c < this.firsts[ai + 1]) {
                if (this.controls[c].on) { any = true; }
                c = c + 1;
            }
            if (any != this.combined[ai]) {
                if (any) { this.onEdge[ai] = true; } else { this.offEdge[ai] = true; }
                this.combined[ai] = any;
            }
            a = a + 1;
        }
    }

    // An entry naming no dead zone of its own takes the defaults: the stick's, radial, as its first filter where it
    // reads both axes of one stick as its x and y; else each stick axis and trigger it reads through its own.
    fn void zoneDefaults(Entry made, isize first) {
        bool pair = false;
        if (made.shape == Shape::Axes2 && made.firsts[1] - made.firsts[0] == 1 && made.firsts[2] - made.firsts[1] == 1) {
            Source x = this.sources[made.firsts[0]];
            Source y = this.sources[made.firsts[1]];
            pair = x.kind == SampleKind::Axis && y.kind == SampleKind::Axis && x.control / 2 == y.control / 2
                && x.control != y.control;
        }
        if (pair) {
            match (this.stickZone) {
                case Some(value: f): {
                    this.filters.add(item: f);
                    this.smoothSteps.add(item: Vec3.zero());
                    this.smoothShown.add(item: Vec3.zero());
                }
                case None: { }
            };
            return;
        }
        isize i = first;
        while (i < this.sources.length()) {
            Source s = this.sources[i];
            if (s.kind == SampleKind::Axis) { this.sources[i].zone = Zone::Stick; }
            if (s.kind == SampleKind::Travel && (s.control == cast<int32>(PadButton::LeftTrigger) || s.control == cast<int32>(PadButton::RightTrigger))) {
                this.sources[i].zone = Zone::Trigger;
            }
            i = i + 1;
        }
    }

    // An entry's filters into the binder's, each held to its range: false, with every refusal added, when any is
    // refused.
    fn bool takeFilters(const ref ControlEntry entry, bool motion, const ref string whose, ref BindingError no) {
        bool fine = true;
        foreach (const ref FilterRecord read in entry.filters().iterConst()) {
            FilterRecord f = read;
            string why = filterRefusal(f: f, points: entry.curvePoints(), motion: motion);
            if (!why.isEmpty()) {
                no.add(line: whose + " " + why);
                fine = false;
                continue;
            }
            if (f.points) {
                isize from = this.points.length();
                isize k = f.pointsFrom;
                while (k < f.pointsTo) {
                    this.points.add(item: entry.curvePoints()[k]);
                    k = k + 1;
                }
                f.pointsFrom = from;
                f.pointsTo = this.points.length();
            }
            this.filters.add(item: f);
            this.smoothSteps.add(item: Vec3.zero());
            this.smoothShown.add(item: Vec3.zero());
        }
        return fine;
    }

    // One device's entry of a digital action's binding: each control it names, resolved by `@kama/window`'s own names.
    fn void bindEntry(const ref string action, Device device, const ref Optional<ControlEntry> entry, ref BindingError no) {
        string where = deviceName(device: device);
        match (entry) {
            case None: { }
            case Some(value: e): {
                if (e.isObject()) {
                    no.add(line: "the " + where + " binding of `" + action + "` is an object, which for a `Digital` holds filters and gestures, KYR-54's later parts: bind a control's name, or a list of them");
                    return;
                }
                foreach (const ref string name in e.names().iterConst()) {
                    Result<int32, Owned<Error>> found = controlOf(device: device, name: name);
                    match (found) {
                        case Ok(value: n): { this.controls.add(item: Bound.make(device: device, control: n)); }
                        case Err(error: e): {
                            string why = e.message();
                            no.add(line: "the " + where + " binding of `" + action + "` names `" + name + "`, which is no " + where + " control: " + why);
                        }
                    };
                }
            }
        };
    }

    // A value action's binding: each device's entry, refused where its kind cannot read it.
    fn void bindValue(ActionKind kind, int32 index, const ref string name, bool delta,
                      const ref SortedMap<string, BindingRecord> bindings, ref BindingError no) {
        if (!bindings.contains(key: name)) { return; }
        borrow bindings.getRef(key: name) as b {
            this.bindValueEntry(kind: kind, index: index, action: name, delta: delta, device: Device::Keyboard, entry: b.keyboard(), no: no);
            this.bindValueEntry(kind: kind, index: index, action: name, delta: delta, device: Device::Mouse, entry: b.mouse(), no: no);
            this.bindValueEntry(kind: kind, index: index, action: name, delta: delta, device: Device::Gamepad, entry: b.gamepad(), no: no);
        }
    }

    // One device's entry of a value action: its shape from its parts, and a source for each control a part names.
    fn void bindValueEntry(ActionKind kind, int32 index, const ref string action, bool delta, Device device,
                           const ref Optional<ControlEntry> entry, ref BindingError no) {
        string where = deviceName(device: device);
        string kindWord = valueKindWord(kind: kind);
        string whose = "the " + where + " binding of `" + action + "`";
        match (entry) {
            case None: { }
            case Some(value: e): {
                if (e.steps().length() > 0) {
                    no.add(line: whose + " names gestures, which KYR-54's later part reads");
                    return;
                }
                DynamicArray<string> words = DynamicArray.empty();
                Shape shape = Shape::One;
                if (e.isObject()) {
                    string why = "";
                    shape = shapeOf(kind: kind, entry: e, why: why);
                    if (!why.isEmpty()) {
                        no.add(line: whose + " " + why);
                        return;
                    }
                    words = partWords(kind: kind, shape: shape);
                } else if (kind != ActionKind::Analog) {
                    if (kind == ActionKind::Vector2 && device == Device::Mouse && e.names().length() == 1 && e.names()[0] == "Motion") {
                        shape = Shape::Axes2;
                    } else {
                        string parts = kind == ActionKind::Vector2 ? "`up`, `down`, `left`, `right`, or `x` and `y`, or the mouse's `Motion`"
                                                                   : "`up`, `down`, `left`, `right`, `forward`, `backward`, or `x`, `y` and `z`";
                        no.add(line: whose + " names a control, and a `" + kindWord + "` is bound by its parts: an object of " + parts);
                        return;
                    }
                }
                Entry made = Entry.make(kind: kind, action: index, shape: shape);
                isize motions = 0;
                isize held = 0;
                isize first = this.sources.length();
                int32 k = 0;
                while (k < 6) {
                    made.firsts[cast<isize>(k)] = this.sources.length();
                    if (cast<isize>(k) < partCount(shape: shape)) {
                        DynamicArray<string> named = namesOf(entry: e, shape: shape, part: k, words: words);
                        foreach (const ref string n in named.iterConst()) {
                            string why = "";
                            Optional<Source> found = valueSourceOf(device: device, name: n, why: why);
                            match (found) {
                                case Some(value: src): {
                                    if (src.kind == SampleKind::Motion) { motions = motions + 1; } else { held = held + 1; }
                                    this.sources.add(item: src);
                                }
                                case None: { no.add(line: whose + " names `" + n + "`, which is no " + where + " control: " + why); }
                            };
                        }
                    }
                    k = k + 1;
                }
                made.firsts[6] = this.sources.length();
                if (motions > 0 && held > 0) {
                    no.add(line: whose + " mixes the mouse's motion, a distance moved, with controls held: bind them in two entries' devices, or to two actions");
                    return;
                }
                if (motions > 0 && !delta) {
                    no.add(line: whose + " names the mouse's motion, a distance moved, so `" + action + "` must be a delta: its record says `\"delta\": true`");
                    return;
                }
                if (motions > 0 && (shape == Shape::Keys2 || shape == Shape::Keys3)) {
                    no.add(line: whose + " names the mouse's motion as a key's part: bind it as `x` and `y`, or as `Motion`");
                    return;
                }
                if (this.sources.length() == first) { return; }
                made.motion = motions > 0;
                made.filterFrom = this.filters.length();
                if (!ownsZone(entry: e)) { this.zoneDefaults(made: made, first: first); }
                bool kept = this.takeFilters(entry: e, motion: made.motion, whose: whose, no: no);
                made.filterTo = this.filters.length();
                if (!kept) { return; }
                this.entries.add(item: made);
            }
        };
    }
}

fn float32 absOf(float32 x) { return x < 0.0 ? -x : x; }
fn float32 signOf(float32 x) { return x > 0.0 ? 1.0 : (x < 0.0 ? -1.0 : 0.0); }

// `x` turned over where `by` is -1; 0 stays 0.
fn float32 invertedBy(float32 x, float32 by) { return by < 0.0 ? 0.0 - x : x; }

// `x`'s size raised to `e`, its sign kept.
fn float32 powered(float32 x, float32 e) {
    if (e == 1.0 || x == 0.0) { return x; }
    float32 a = pow(x: absOf(x: x), y: e);
    return x < 0.0 ? 0.0 - a : a;
}

fn float32 remapped(float32 x, FilterRecord f) { return f.c + (x - f.a) / (f.b - f.a) * (f.d - f.c); }

// `v` on its first `dims` axes, the others 0.
fn Vec3 masked(Vec3 v, int32 dims) {
    return Vec3.of(x: v.x, y: dims >= 2 ? v.y : 0.0, z: dims >= 3 ? v.z : 0.0);
}

fn Vec3 unit(Vec3 v) {
    float32 l2 = lengthSquared(v: v);
    if (l2 == 0.0) { return v; }
    float32 l = sqrt(x: l2);
    return Vec3.of(x: v.x / l, y: v.y / l, z: v.z / l);
}

// A dead zone's one number: 0 inside its lower end; past its upper, 1 scaled or the upper end itself unscaled; between,
// rescaled from 0 to 1 or kept.
fn float32 zoned(float32 size, FilterRecord f) {
    if (size <= f.a) { return 0.0; }
    if (size >= f.b) { return f.scaled ? 1.0 : f.b; }
    return f.scaled ? (size - f.a) / (f.b - f.a) : size;
}

// `v` through a dead zone: on its length, its direction kept, or on each axis apart.
fn Vec3 deadZoned(Vec3 v, FilterRecord f) {
    if (f.radial) {
        float32 l2 = lengthSquared(v: v);
        if (l2 == 0.0) { return v; }
        float32 l = sqrt(x: l2);
        float32 to = zoned(size: l, f: f);
        return Vec3.of(x: v.x / l * to, y: v.y / l * to, z: v.z / l * to);
    }
    return Vec3.of(x: signOf(x: v.x) * zoned(size: absOf(x: v.x), f: f), y: signOf(x: v.y) * zoned(size: absOf(x: v.y), f: f),
                   z: signOf(x: v.z) * zoned(size: absOf(x: v.z), f: f));
}

// `v` held to a clamp: each axis between its least and its most, or its length to the longest.
fn Vec3 clampedBy(Vec3 v, FilterRecord f) {
    if (f.byLength) {
        float32 l2 = lengthSquared(v: v);
        if (l2 <= f.c * f.c) { return v; }
        float32 l = sqrt(x: l2);
        return Vec3.of(x: v.x / l * f.c, y: v.y / l * f.c, z: v.z / l * f.c);
    }
    return Vec3.of(x: clampedOne(x: v.x, f: f), y: clampedOne(x: v.y, f: f), z: clampedOne(x: v.z, f: f));
}

fn float32 clampedOne(float32 x, FilterRecord f) {
    float32 low = f.hasA && x < f.a ? f.a : x;
    return f.hasB && low > f.b ? f.b : low;
}

// Whether an entry's own filters name a dead zone, which takes the place of the defaults.
fn bool ownsZone(const ref ControlEntry entry) {
    foreach (const ref FilterRecord f in entry.filters().iterConst()) {
        if (f.kind == FilterKind::DeadZone) { return true; }
    }
    return false;
}

fn string filterWord(FilterKind kind) {
    return match (kind) {
        case DeadZone: "deadZone"; case Scale: "scale"; case Invert: "invert"; case Curve: "curve"; case Clamp: "clamp";
        case Remap: "remap"; case Normalize: "normalize"; case Digital: "digital"; case Smooth: "smooth";
        case Threshold: "threshold";
    };
}

// Why a value entry's filter `f` is refused, or "": a filter the mouse's motion cannot take, a threshold, which makes a
// button, or a number out of its range.
fn string filterRefusal(const ref FilterRecord f, const ref DynamicArray<float32> points, bool motion) {
    string word = filterWord(kind: f.kind);
    bool linear = match (f.kind) { case Scale: true; case Invert: true; case Smooth: true; case _: false; };
    if (motion && !linear) {
        return "puts a `" + word + "` on the mouse's motion, a distance moved, which would change with the step's length: only `scale`, `invert` and `smooth` filter it";
    }
    float32 a = f.a;
    float32 b = f.b;
    match (f.kind) {
        case Threshold: { return "lists a `threshold`: a `threshold` makes a button from a value, so it filters a `Digital`'s entry"; }
        case DeadZone: {
            if (a < 0.0) { return "has a dead zone: its `lower`, ${a}, must be 0 or more"; }
            if (a >= b) { return "has a dead zone: its `lower`, ${a}, must be below its `upper`, ${b}"; }
        }
        case Curve: {
            if (f.points) {
                if (f.pointsTo - f.pointsFrom < 4) { return "has a `curve` of one point: a `curve` through points needs two or more"; }
                isize k = f.pointsFrom + 2;
                while (k < f.pointsTo) {
                    if (points[k] <= points[k - 2]) { return "has a `curve` whose inputs fall or repeat: a `curve`'s points must rise in input"; }
                    k = k + 2;
                }
            } else if (a <= 0.0 || b <= 0.0 || f.c <= 0.0) {
                return "has a `curve` of no rise: a `curve`'s exponent must be more than 0";
            }
        }
        case Clamp: {
            if (!f.hasA && !f.hasB && !f.byLength) { return "has an empty `clamp`: a `clamp` names its `min`, its `max` or its `length`"; }
            if (f.hasA && f.hasB && a > b) { return "has a `clamp` past itself: a `clamp`'s `min` must be at most its `max`"; }
            if (f.byLength && f.c <= 0.0) { return "has a `clamp` of no length: a `clamp`'s `length` must be more than 0"; }
        }
        case Remap: {
            if (a == b) { return "has a `remap` from one number: a `remap`'s `from` must span a range"; }
        }
        case Smooth: {
            if (a <= 0.0) { return "has a `smooth` of no time: a `smooth`'s seconds must be more than 0"; }
        }
        case _: { }
    };
    return "";
}
fn float32 lengthSquared(Vec3 v) { return v.x * v.x + v.y * v.y + v.z * v.z; }

// A direction no longer than 1: keys pressed together, a diagonal.
fn Vec3 clamped(Vec3 v) {
    float32 l2 = lengthSquared(v: v);
    if (l2 <= 1.0) { return v; }
    float32 l = sqrt(x: l2);
    return Vec3.of(x: v.x / l, y: v.y / l, z: v.z / l);
}

// The kind of the action named `name`, as a records file writes it, or "" when the game declares none of that name.
fn string kindOf(const ref ActionList actions, const ref string name) {
    if (actions.digitalNames().contains(item: name)) { return "Digital"; }
    if (actions.analogNames().contains(item: name)) { return "Analog"; }
    if (actions.vector2Names().contains(item: name)) { return "Vector2"; }
    if (actions.vector3Names().contains(item: name)) { return "Vector3"; }
    if (actions.poseNames().contains(item: name)) { return "Pose"; }
    return "";
}

fn string valueKindWord(ActionKind kind) {
    return match (kind) { case Analog: "Analog"; case Vector2: "Vector2"; case Vector3: "Vector3"; case _: "value"; };
}

fn string deviceName(Device device) {
    return match (device) { case Keyboard: "keyboard"; case Mouse: "mouse"; case Gamepad: "gamepad"; };
}

// How many parts a shape reads.
fn isize partCount(Shape shape) {
    return match (shape) { case One: 1; case Pair: 2; case Keys2: 4; case Axes2: 2; case Keys3: 6; case Axes3: 3; };
}

// The words of a shape's parts, in their order.
fn DynamicArray<string> partWords(ActionKind kind, Shape shape) {
    DynamicArray<string> w = DynamicArray.empty();
    match (shape) {
        case One: { }
        case Pair: { w.add(item: "positive"); w.add(item: "negative"); }
        case Keys2: { w.add(item: "up"); w.add(item: "down"); w.add(item: "left"); w.add(item: "right"); }
        case Axes2: { w.add(item: "x"); w.add(item: "y"); }
        case Keys3: {
            w.add(item: "up"); w.add(item: "down"); w.add(item: "left"); w.add(item: "right"); w.add(item: "forward");
            w.add(item: "backward");
        }
        case Axes3: { w.add(item: "x"); w.add(item: "y"); w.add(item: "z"); }
    };
    return w;
}

// The shape an object entry's words make for `kind`, or why they make none (`why` set).
fn Shape shapeOf(ActionKind kind, const ref ControlEntry entry, ref string why) {
    bool keys = false;
    bool axes = false;
    bool pair = false;
    string unknown = "";
    foreach (string w in entry.parts()) {
        if (w == "positive" || w == "negative") { pair = true; }
        else if (w == "up" || w == "down" || w == "left" || w == "right" || w == "forward" || w == "backward") { keys = true; }
        else if (w == "x" || w == "y" || w == "z") { axes = true; }
        else if (unknown.isEmpty()) { unknown = copy w; }
        if ((w == "forward" || w == "backward" || w == "z") && kind != ActionKind::Vector3 && unknown.isEmpty()) { unknown = copy w; }
    }
    string allowed = match (kind) {
        case Analog: "`positive` and `negative`";
        case Vector2: "`up`, `down`, `left` and `right`, or `x` and `y`";
        case Vector3: "`up`, `down`, `left`, `right`, `forward` and `backward`, or `x`, `y` and `z`";
        case _: "none";
    };
    string kindWord = valueKindWord(kind: kind);
    if (!unknown.isEmpty() || (kind == ActionKind::Analog && (keys || axes)) || (kind != ActionKind::Analog && pair)) {
        string named = unknown.isEmpty() ? "a part" : "`" + unknown + "`";
        why = "names " + named + ", which is no part of a `" + kindWord + "`: its parts are " + allowed;
        return Shape::One;
    }
    if (keys && axes) {
        why = "names both keys' parts and axes: a `" + kindWord + "`'s entry is one or the other, " + allowed;
        return Shape::One;
    }
    if (!keys && !axes && !pair) {
        why = "is an object naming no part: a `" + kindWord + "`'s parts are " + allowed;
        return Shape::One;
    }
    if (pair) { return Shape::Pair; }
    if (kind == ActionKind::Vector2) { return keys ? Shape::Keys2 : Shape::Axes2; }
    return keys ? Shape::Keys3 : Shape::Axes3;
}

// The names a part of an entry reads: an entry written as a name or a list reads them all as its one part; the mouse's
// `Motion` reads its two axes; an object's part reads what its word names, none when it names none.
fn DynamicArray<string> namesOf(const ref ControlEntry entry, Shape shape, int32 part, const ref DynamicArray<string> words) {
    DynamicArray<string> named = DynamicArray.empty();
    if (!entry.isObject()) {
        if (shape == Shape::Axes2) {
            named.add(item: part == 0 ? "MotionX" : "MotionY");
            return named;
        }
        foreach (const ref string n in entry.names().iterConst()) { named.add(item: copy n); }
        return named;
    }
    string word = copy words[cast<isize>(part)];
    if (!entry.parts().contains(key: word)) { return named; }
    foreach (const ref string n in entry.parts().getRef(key: word).iterConst()) { named.add(item: copy n); }
    return named;
}

// A digital control's number from its name, read by `@kama/window`'s own reader for its device: a `Key`'s USB HID usage
// id, a `PointerButton`'s W3C button, a `PadButton`'s W3C standard index. The reader's refusal lists every name.
fn Result<int32, Owned<Error>> controlOf(Device device, const ref string name) {
    string quoted = "\"" + name + "\"";
    match (device) {
        case Keyboard: {
            Result<Key, Owned<Error>> k = deserializeJsonBuffer::<Key>(src: copy quoted, strict: true);
            match (give k) {
                case Ok(value: v): { return Result::Ok(value: cast<int32>(v)); }
                case Err(error: e): { return Result::Err(error: give e); }
            };
        }
        case Mouse: {
            Result<PointerButton, Owned<Error>> b = deserializeJsonBuffer::<PointerButton>(src: copy quoted, strict: true);
            match (give b) {
                case Ok(value: v): { return Result::Ok(value: cast<int32>(v)); }
                case Err(error: e): { return Result::Err(error: give e); }
            };
        }
        case Gamepad: {
            Result<PadButton, Owned<Error>> p = deserializeJsonBuffer::<PadButton>(src: copy quoted, strict: true);
            match (give p) {
                case Ok(value: v): { return Result::Ok(value: cast<int32>(v)); }
                case Err(error: e): { return Result::Err(error: give e); }
            };
        }
    };
}


// A value's control from its name, or none with `why` set: a key, a mouse button or a pad button's edge or travel by
// `@kama/window`'s readers, a pad's stick axis by `PadAxis` (its Y turned over), or the mouse's `MotionX` or `MotionY`
// (its Y turned over). A reader's refusal lists every name.
fn Optional<Source> valueSourceOf(Device device, const ref string name, ref string why) {
    string quoted = "\"" + name + "\"";
    match (device) {
        case Keyboard: {
            Result<int32, Owned<Error>> k = controlOf(device: device, name: name);
            match (give k) {
                case Ok(value: v): { return Optional::Some(value: Source.make(device: device, kind: SampleKind::Control, control: v, flip: false)); }
                case Err(error: e): {
                    why = e.message();
                    return Optional::None;
                }
            };
        }
        case Mouse: {
            if (name == "MotionX") { return Optional::Some(value: Source.make(device: device, kind: SampleKind::Motion, control: 0, flip: false)); }
            if (name == "MotionY") { return Optional::Some(value: Source.make(device: device, kind: SampleKind::Motion, control: 1, flip: true)); }
            Result<int32, Owned<Error>> b = controlOf(device: device, name: name);
            match (give b) {
                case Ok(value: v): { return Optional::Some(value: Source.make(device: device, kind: SampleKind::Control, control: v, flip: false)); }
                case Err(error: e): {
                    string asButton = e.message();
                    why = asButton + "; nor the mouse's motion, `MotionX` or `MotionY`";
                    return Optional::None;
                }
            };
        }
        case Gamepad: {
            Result<PadButton, Owned<Error>> p = deserializeJsonBuffer::<PadButton>(src: copy quoted, strict: true);
            match (give p) {
                case Ok(value: v): {
                    return Optional::Some(value: Source.make(device: device, kind: SampleKind::Travel, control: cast<int32>(v), flip: false));
                }
                case Err(error: e): {
                    string asButton = e.message();
                    Result<PadAxis, Owned<Error>> x = deserializeJsonBuffer::<PadAxis>(src: copy quoted, strict: true);
                    match (give x) {
                        case Ok(value: axis): {
                            bool turned = axis == PadAxis::LeftY || axis == PadAxis::RightY;
                            return Optional::Some(value: Source.make(device: device, kind: SampleKind::Axis, control: cast<int32>(axis), flip: turned));
                        }
                        case Err(error: f): {
                            string asAxis = f.message();
                            why = "no button (" + asButton + ") and no stick's axis (" + asAxis + ")";
                            return Optional::None;
                        }
                    };
                }
            };
        }
    };
}
